      "text": "Let's start by analyzing the given information and the diagram. We know that \\( RSP \\) is a straight line, which means that \\( \\angle RSP = 180^\\circ \\). We are also given that \\( \\angle QSP = 80^\\circ \\).\n\nFirst, we need to find the measure of \\( \\angle QSR \\). Since \\( \\angle QSP \\) and \\( \\angle QSR \\) form a straight line at point \\( S \\), their sum is \\( 180^\\circ \\). Therefore, we can write:\n\\[\n\\angle QSP + \\angle QSR = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSubstituting the given value of \\( \\angle QSP \\):\n\\[\n80^\\circ + \\angle QSR = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\( \\angle QSR \\):\n\\[\n\\angle QSR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the measure of \\( \\angle PQR \\). Notice that \\( \\angle PQR \\) and \\( \\angle QSP \\) form a linear pair at point \\( R \\) because they are adjacent angles on a straight line. Therefore, their sum is \\( 180^\\circ \\). So, we can write:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR + \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSubstituting the given value of \\( \\angle QSP \\):\n\\[\n\\angle PQR + 80^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\( \\angle PQR \\):\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\( \\angle PQR \\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\).",
