      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) in degrees given that \\(RSP\\) is a straight line and \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\nFirst, let's analyze the given information and the diagram. We know that \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, which means that the sum of \\(\\angle QSP\\) and \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(180^\\circ\\). Here's the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, the total angle at point \\(S\\) on the line is \\(180^\\circ\\).\n2. We are given that \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n3. Let \\(\\angle PQR = x\\) degrees. Since the sum of the angles around point \\(S\\) is \\(180^\\circ\\), we can write the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\angle QSP + \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Substituting the given value of \\(\\angle QSP\\):\n   \\[\n   80^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n4. Solving for \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   x = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\) degrees.",
