      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) given the information about \\(\\angle QSP\\) and the properties of the angles in the figure.\n\n1. **Identify the given angles:**\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\)\n\n2. **Understand the properties of the angles:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, so the angles around point \\(S\\) on the straight line sum up to \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Determine the angle \\(\\angle PQS\\):**\n   - Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, \\(\\angle PQS\\) is supplementary to \\(\\angle QSP\\). Therefore, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQS = 180^\\circ - \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n4. **Use the fact that \\(PQR\\) and \\(QRS\\) are supplementary:**\n   - \\(\\angle PQR\\) and \\(\\angle QRS\\) are supplementary because they form a straight line. Therefore, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQR + \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n5. **Find the measure of \\(\\angle QRS\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle QRS\\) is the same as \\(\\angle RQS\\) because they are straight angles.\n   - Since \\(\\angle RQS = \\angle PQS - \\angle QSP\\) (as \\(\\angle PQS\\) is composed of \\(\\angle RQS\\) and \\(\\angle QSP\\)), we have:\n     \\[\n     \\angle RQS = \\angle PQS - \\angle QSP = 100^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 20^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n6. **Calculate \\(\\angle PQR\\):**\n   - Using the relationship between \\(\\angle PQR\\) and \\(\\angle QRS\\), we get:\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ - 20^\\circ = 160^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{160}\\).",
