      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given information and the geometric relationships in the diagram. We know that \\(RSP\\) is a straight line and that \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\). We need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\).\n\nFirst, let's determine the measure of \\(\\angle QPS\\). Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, the sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle QSP + \\angle QPS = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nGiven that \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\), we can substitute this value into the equation:\n\\[\n80^\\circ + \\angle QPS = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\angle QPS\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\angle QPS = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\). Notice that \\(\\angle PQR\\) is an exterior angle to \\(\\triangle QPS\\). The exterior angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the two non-adjacent interior angles. Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = \\angle QPS + \\angle QSP\n\\]\nSubstituting the values we know, we get:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = 100^\\circ + 80^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nHowever, we need to re-evaluate the setup. The correct approach is to recognize that \\(\\angle PQR\\) is an exterior angle to \\(\\triangle QPS\\) and is actually the straight angle minus the adjacent interior angle \\(\\angle QPS\\). Since \\(\\angle QPS\\) is actually the angle we are subtracting from the straight angle, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - \\angle QPS = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{40}\n\\]",
